                                    <p class="ecl-u-type-paragraph">In this episode we are talking about living in the EU’s countryside. Rural areas are often misunderstood. For some, they're romantic havens from the stress of city life. For others, they're tough places to get work, healthcare, and education. So, what do data reveal about rural living in the EU?</p>

<p class="ecl-u-type-paragraph">3 experts from the European Commission will tell us more: Marina Royo de Blas, programme assistant at the Directorate-General for Agriculture and Rural Development, working on the long-term vision for rural areas in Europe; Reka Fodor from Eurostat, who edited the recently released Urban Europe and Rural Europe publications; and Lewis Dijkstra who leads the Urban Territorial Analysis team at the Joint Research Centre. Together with Jonathan Elliot they will look at the data about rural Europe and try to tease out the stories behind the numbers.</p>
